From eb255ccc9c0a2655cfd42262b7fe1b147c216c8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:53:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] arm: dts: add Amlogic S6 SoC device tree

Add the Amlogic S6 SoC device tree from the Linux tree used with the
board, together with its reset IDs header, as dts/upstream only has a
minimal amlogic-s6.dtsi without the clock controllers, MMC and Ethernet
nodes.

The U-Boot additions in amlogic-s6-u-boot.dtsi:
- describe the firmware owned fixed PLL, sys and axi clocks (SCMI on
  Linux) as fixed-rate clocks feeding the PLL and peripherals clock
  controllers,
- mark the console path (xtal, buses, pin controller, UART B and its
  pins) for pre-relocation,
- describe the dwmac 4.x Ethernet MAC with the "amlogic,s6-dwmac"
  compatible handled by the Meson DWC Ethernet QoS glue and enable the
  MDIO multiplexer gate together with the MAC clocks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
